What is the largest spread between dr=92s that the Nupi can be used on? Can=
 you do dr 9 to dr 17?

From: John Riordan [mailto:JRiordan@harcofittings.com]
Sent: Friday, December 09, 2011 9:58 AM
To: Debra Driskill; Denise DeLoatch; Janet McNamee; Justin Patchett; Karen =
Taylor; Kathy Moore; Mary Tyree; Shelley Jennings; Tony Womack; Brian Hurle=
y; Curtis Bruton; Dirk Merrill; Ed Eichmann; 'Jack Harrington'; John Fralic=
k; Mike Friedman; Mike Scheel; Phil Busman
Cc: Mike Harrington
Subject: Product Info BLURT #6: Nupi EF Couplings fusing across a joint wit=
h different DR's

Hello All,

It is acceptable to use an electrofusion coupling to fuse two pipes with di=
fferent DR=92s.  For instance DR17 to DR11.

In fact it is preferred that an electrofusion coupling is used to fuse two =
different DR=92s together rather than butt fusing.

Recall that there is a limit with the Nupi that the standard fusion cycle n=
ot be used on pipe thinner than DR17.  See Info Blurt #5.

John

